<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolzano</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bozen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bolzano, in German Bozen, is the capital of the autonomous province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-tyrol">South Tyrol</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, where the Talfer meets the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eisack">Eisack</a>. A market town on the route over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brenner-pass">Brenner Pass</a>, it belonged to the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrol">Tyrol</a> and passed to Italy after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. Its museum holds Ötzi, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">Copper</a> Age iceman found in 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bolzano.jpg" alt="Bolzano" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bartleby08 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bozen-Bolzano_from_the_Oswaldpromenade.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
